<div class="heading">D&nbsp;O&nbsp;W&nbsp;N&nbsp;L&nbsp;O&nbsp;A&nbsp;D</div>
<br/><br/>


<FORM ACTION="customize.asp" METHOD=get><INPUT CLASS=nav TYPE=submit VALUE="Configure Timers" ONFOCUS="blur()"></FORM>
<P>Version 4.0 features a new type of timer with lots of customization options. Click the "Configure Timers" button to select options for your custom download package.<BR><BR>
<B>Timer Features</B>
<UL>

<LI>The marker can be set with a single click. Simply click on the location where you want the marker and it will automatically jump to the spot where you clicked.<BR><BR></LI>
<LI>Specify the name and duration for each timer to match the events you want to time. For easy identification, you can assign any spell/item icon in the game to each timer and choose from 12 colors for each timer bar.<BR><BR></LI>
<LI>Each timer's name and duration appears as a tooltip when you hover your mouse over the timer's icon.<BR><BR></LI><IMG SRC="image/screenshot/tooltip.png"><BR><BR>
<LI>To begin timing an event, just set the marker to the current position of the dot. The dot will continue moving and reach the marker's position again when exactly one duration of the timer has elapsed. As the dot approaches the marker, you will know that time's almost up.<BR><BR></LI>
<LI>For timing variable-duration events, tick marks on the timer bar make it easy to set the marker and see the amount of time left.<BR><BR></LI>
<LI>If you wish, you can add additional pages of timers so you can use different timer configurations for different situations.<BR><BR></LI><IMG SRC="image/screenshot/tabs.png"><BR><BR>
<LI>Include up to 8 timers in your configuration, or up to 12 timers divided between tabbed pages. You can configure up to 4 tabbed pages of timers.<BR><BR></LI>
<LI>The timer bar can be one of 13 different sizes. Choose a larger timer for better granularity or choose a smaller timer to conserve screen space.<BR><BR></LI><IMG SRC="image/screenshot/large.png"> <IMG SRC="image/screenshot/small.png"><BR><BR>
<LI>Customize the layout of your timers by specifying the number of columns and rows. The timers can be horizontal or vertical, and the icon can be placed on either end of the timer bar. If you wish, you can also specify the spacing between timers.<BR><BR></LI><IMG SRC="image/screenshot/vertical.png"> <IMG SRC="image/screenshot/spacing.png"><BR><BR>
<LI>For each timer, you can choose between two marker styles. A standard marker can be set by clicking anywhere on the bar, and is good for timing events that only have a single instance, such as abilities and some spells. A split marker contains two halves that are set independently of each other by clicking on the corresponding half of the bar. Split markers allow you to time two instances of the same event, for example, staggering costly buffs or mezzing a late add.<BR><BR></LI>
<LI>Choose from 4 different base skins for better integration with your existing UI.<BR><BR></LI>

</UL>


</P>

